    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Crack growth in rock renders rock anisotropic. The degree of anisotropy is explained in terms of effective elastic moduli as a function of load level. In this study, we calculate the changes of elastic moduli due to crack growth numerically by using the crack model and compare these values with experimental results obtained from the measurement of ultrasonic wave velocities. Image processing technique is used to obtain the initial crack information needed for the numerical calculation of elastic moduli. It is shown that non-linear behavior of rock under compression can be predicted by a crack model.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
